{"type":"npc","name":"Beat Hopper","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":60,"temp":0,"max":60,"details":""},"ac":{"value":22,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":40,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":20}],"details":""},"weaknesses":[{"type":"cold-iron","value":5,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"sonic","value":5,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","fey","melodian"],"details":""},"level":{"value":5},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Beat hoppers are rare fey whose performances affect the internal clocks of creatures hearing them. Their long, grasshopper-like bodies and powerful legs allow them to make percussive beats, which they accompany with their smooth singing voices.</p><p>Beat hoppers are typically pacifistic, good-natured, and fun-loving, but they severely lack common sense when it comes to the timing of their performances, which can cause them to become inadvertent instigators. The time-altering music that beat hoppers play with their legs affects friends and enemies equally, so things can become truly chaotic when a beat hopper decides to perform a lively tune during a tavern brawl.</p><p>Most beat hoppers are attuned to three different tempos, each of which matches one of their magical performances. Trying to use a tempo that is drastically faster or slower than their familiar beats is dangerous for a beat hopper, as their hearts synchronize to the music's rhythm. Beat hoppers can learn to do so by dedicating over a century to the careful training of the body and song. Those who manage this feat are known as beat hopper maestros. Maestros deepen their mastery of occult magic and expand the range of spells that they can augment with their inexorable beats.</p><h2>Ill Timing</h2><p>For creatures so attuned to variations in timing, beat hoppers have a surprisingly abysmal grasp of the future. They're poor planners when it comes to putting aside the necessities of life, and they often encourage others to adopt a similar come-what-may attitude. When a beat hopper sees people working together to bring in a harvest or to prepare defenses against an impending attack, the beat hopper might encourage workers to take \"just a little time out\" for a quick dance or ten. Without intending the slightest bit of harm, a beat hopper can easily bring ruin to a community.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 18/45/80 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (slashing), armor (light, medium), skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Diplomacy, Nature, Occultism, Performance)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, charisma, dexterity, energy resistant (sonic, vitality), intelligence, mind, mind shield, music, sensory (low-light vision), spells (Occult: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.3JG1t3T4mWn6vTke]{Blur}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.KqvqNAfGIE5a9wSv]{Heroism}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.wzLkNU3AAqOSKFPR]{Noise Blast}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.DCQHaLrYXMI37dvW]{Paralyze}, @UUID[Compendium.battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.spells.PF3gWKYvNgb56kaI]{Songshroud}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.60sgbuMWN0268dB7]{Telekinetic Projectile}), time, wild, winged</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Jesse Lehto","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":2},"dex":{"mod":5},"con":{"mod":2},"int":{"mod":3},"wis":{"mod":2},"cha":{"mod":5}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":13,"senses":[{"type":"low-light-vision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":9,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":14,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":13,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":12,"special":[]},"athletics":{"base":11,"special":[{"label":"to Long Jump","predicate":["action:long-jump"],"base":13}]},"diplomacy":{"base":12,"special":[]},"nature":{"base":11,"special":[]},"occultism":{"base":12,"special":[]},"performance":{"base":13,"special":[]}},"traits":{"value":["fey"],"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"sm"}}},"_id":"nLH70MUha0HBFJAD","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/beat-hopper.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Beat Hopper","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":1,"height":1,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/beat-hopper.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1.6,"scaleY":1.6,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":[],"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":2,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/subjects/beat-hopper.webp"}},"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"randomImg":false,"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null},"items":[{"type":"action","name":"Friend To All","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"description":{"value":"<p>By default, all creatures are considered allies to the beat hopper for the composition spells. A creature can attempt a @Check[will|dc:22] save at the start of its turn to avoid being treated as the bea